{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And the days of Yitzchak were, etc.</b> The reason Scripture did not mention \"life\" in connection with Yitzchak, as is its custom with Avraham and Yaakov — and even with Yosef it mentioned life, as it is written (Genesis 50:22) ״וַיְחִי יוֹסֵף״ — is perhaps that since from the day he was born until the Akedah he had no wife, and they of blessed memory said (Kohelet Rabbah 9) that one who dwells without a wife dwells without life, and from the time of the Akedah onward they of blessed memory said (Bereishit Rabbah 65) that his eyes began to dim — therefore it did not mention life in connection with him." "<b>Or</b> it is possible, since he did not bring life with him until the Akedah, Scripture did not mention life in connection with him."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:46:10.989854112Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}